#define CT_CRONO_CRIT_RET_ARM  92 // A -> `98 02 19` armed (IP CE/D781: cap1 f148 with A=30, cap2 f172 A=33)
#define CT_CRONO_CRIT_RET_GAP   2 // arm -> the FIRST position change (A+94: cap1 f150, cap2 f174)
#define CT_CRONO_CRIT_SNAP_HOLD 8 // R -> the `1B 19` snap (cap1 R=130 -> 138; cap2 R=136 -> 144)
#define CT_CRONO_CRIT_SPANEND 146 // A -> $A013<-0 (cap1 A=30 -> 176, cap2 A=33 -> 179). The universal
                                //   decomposition still holds: WINDUP = A+83 (the `50` popup birth) + 58 + 5.
#define CT_CRONO_CRIT_STRIKE2 59 // A -> beat-B (the SECOND slash). Its wash peaks A+61 in 2 of 3 captures
                                //   (A+62 only in cap1), and the slash-2 STRIKE pose is A+59 in both of
                                //   those -- so the canonical event is A+59. Flash-only (no re-strike).
                                //   WAS 91 from DISPATCH, i.e. 19-A frames off, growing with the leap.
// GATO (A3.1 rear-up + claw-swipe, HOLD timeline): the rear-up (kf8 G1_rearup) starts at dispatch (oracle
// f505 = rel 0), held ~49f; the flash lands on the target (Crono) at f532 = rel 27; GATO returns to idle at
// f554 = rel 49 (A3.2 confirms the pose is timeline-independent). Field.c draws the held rear-up; the
// claw-swipe tile stream (0x80-0x9F) is the anim-engine BOUNDARY (only kf8's rep frame is baked).
#define CT_GATO_STRIKE     27   // rel: rear-up start f505 -> flash-on-Crono f532 (A3.1)
// CT_GATO_WINDOW (rel: rear-up start f505 -> return-to-idle f554, A3.1 = the ANIMATION length; gates
// fxEnemyRearup, GATO idles for the rest of the frozen span below) is now declared in battle.h -- it is
// architecturally the shared "how long ANY enemy's action window animates before it idles" boundary (the
// GATO fight derived its value, but the mechanism is enemy-generic), and field.c's Hetake leap-arc render
// (battle_scenario2.md T1.4) replays its OWN measured trajectory over this SAME window rather than
// inventing a new gameplay-timing constant (battle_loop.md pacing/freeze spans stay untouched).
// ============ THE $A013 ACTION-FREEZE SPAN LAW (battle_loop.md §I; the "too fast" pacing fix) ============
// The freeze DURATION per action = the action's full animation span in REAL render frames (the $993A clock is
// FROZEN during an action, so it is real-frame-paced, NOT the 2.5f/tick logic cadence; §E-§H). §I: the frozen
// span is a `$9876`-gated animation LOOP (C1/4090 loops while $9876==0), and what VARIES its length is the AI-
// chosen ATTACK, held in the selector `$9877` (byte, set ONCE at dispatch, constant through the span, indexes
// anim-length table CD/5FF0). The bank-CC AI+anim interpreter that picks the attack IS the standing S4
// BOUNDARY, so the per-attack lengths are OBSERVED/pinned per (attacker, $9877) below -- the copyFreeze
// precedent (§I: "emergent from script execution, per-attack-pinned"). $9877 writers: PC C1:43FF, GATO the
// $AE93 table switch C1/44AF (C1:44BB attack A / C1:44E7 attack B). We WRITE the real WRAM byte mem[$9877] at
// dispatch and derive the span from it (battleActionSpan); the HP-apply lands on the span's LAST frame (§I:
// C1:ED1A), the visual strike (flash/popup) at the anim strike moment.
// ---- THE UNIVERSAL SPAN LAW (battle_span_emergence.md §0.2, 6/6 oracle-confirmed to the frame) ----
//   span = WINDUP + POPUP(58) + TAIL        TAIL = 5 (PC) / 7 (enemy)
// The span is the RUNTIME of the CD/5FF0 multi-track bytecode interpreter (C1/4CA2, ticked once per real
// frame by the action loop C1/4090 while $A013=1). WINDUP = freeze-on -> op-50 ShowDamage; POPUP = the 58f
// $A3D1 popup life (CT_FX_POPUP_LIFE); TAIL = the popup-gated EndTech->freeze-off handshake (CT_ACT_TAIL_*).
// The POPUP + TAIL + the explicit interpreter 20-pauses are the ROM-derived ENVELOPE; the WINDUP is dominated
// by the 03/06 PLAY one-shot durations (E4/DC ptrB dwell-sums), the enemy PRE-STRIKE, and the PC APPROACH
// travel -- the Stage-1/2/3 pose-engine + mover residual (battle_anim_engine.md §B.1-B.3). So FULL span
// EMERGENCE (retiring these CT_SPAN_* for a live interpreter, dossier §6.2) is UNBLOCKED structurally but
// GATED on Stages 1-3 supplying the play/travel lengths; until then the totals stay OBSERVED/pinned per
// $9877 (the copyFreeze precedent) and the completion MODEL (popup birth + tail) IS the derived §5 mechanism
// (CT_FX_POPUP_LIFE / CT_ACT_TAIL_* above), so the span is now structured, not just a magic number.
// Reconstructions (windup+58+tail): melee 62+58+5=125, crit 114+58+5=177, Marle 84+58+4=146, GATO-A
// 92+58+7=157, GATO-B 157..161+58+7=222..226, song 246+58+7=311.
#define CT_SPAN_PC_NORMAL  125  // $9877=0x00 (Crono melee, C1:4340 close) / 0x03 (Marle CLOSE-melee, span 125,
                                //   battle_polish3.md §3.1): §G/§I ledger f643->768. The dist²<=40² close variant.
#define CT_SPAN_PC_RANGED  137  // $9877=0x02 -> CD/5FF0[0x02]=CD/6E83: MARLE's FAR/ranged crossbow (dist²>40²,
                                //   battle_polish3.md §3.1: span 137, $AEEB=02, −18 -- SAME damage as her close
