  // the shuffles' frame, where C1:B2C3 writes `06 FF FF` -- after them. The port swept here, and the shuffles lost her.)
  // NORMALIZE $A0B3 to 0 (battle_span_emergence.md §1.3, oracle-verified). $A0B3 is the anim-track loader's
  // VARIANT selector (C1/4562: 0 -> mask word 1, !=0 -> word 2). The ROM NEVER stores it nonzero (0 STA/0 INC
  // in the whole ROM; it is only STZ'd in the 5 word-2 loader tails) and the battle-work-RAM init zeroes it,
  // so the oracle reads $A0B3=0 at EVERY dispatch (verified on gato_inbattle.state: GATO-A f0, PC-melee f44
  // C1:43FF, GATO-B f173 C1:44E7 -- all $A0B3=00). Our raw-WRAM staging carries a STALE pre-battle 0x80 (the
  // whole $A0B0-$A0BF work-RAM block reads 0x80 in gato_t0.raw.wram vs the oracle in-battle 00, so the ROM's
  // battle-init block-clear zeroes it); without this the parser would branch to the never-dispatched word-2
  // track set (a PHANTOM 1E in GATO's exec track CD/963E, over-counted tracks). Clear it once here so
  // battleAnimParse reads the same real flag the oracle does -> word 1 (the dossier's per-script truth), no hardcode.
  h->mem[0xA0B3] = 0;
